      "id": "q1-code",
      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Question 1 · C sieve",
      "markdown": "",
      "displayCode": {
        "c": "#include <stdio.h>\n\n#define MAX 100\n\nint isprime[MAX+1];\nint i, j;\n\nint main() {\n  for (i=0; i<=MAX; i++)\n    isprime[i] = 1;\n  for (i=2; i<=MAX; i++)\n    if (isprime[i]) {\n      printf(\"%d\\n\", i);\n\n      j = i*i;\n      while (j <= {{A}}) {\n        isprime[j] = 0;\n        j += {{B}};\n      }\n    }\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q5-code",
      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Question 5 · C program segment",
      "markdown": "",
      "displayCode": {
        "c": "scanf(\"%d%d\", &x, &y);\nfor (i=x; i<=y; i++)\n  printf(\"%d\", i/7);"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q2-code",
      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Question 2 · C selection sort",
      "markdown": "Let A[0..N-1] (A[N] in C Version) be an array of integers. Suppose you are given the following two functions:\n\n- function FindMin(x, y: integer): integer\n  (int FindMin(int x, int y) in C Version)\n  This function returns the index of the smallest element in A[x], A[x+1], … , A[y]. For example, if A[4] is the smallest element among A[3], A[4], A[5] and A[6], then FindMin(3, 6) will return the value 4. The parameters x and y must satisfy 0 ≤ x ≤ y < N.\n- procedure Swap(x, y: integer)\n  (void Swap(int x, int y) in C Version)\n  This function swaps the contents of A[x] and A[y]. The parameters x and y must satisfy 0 ≤ x < N and 0 ≤ y < N. x may equal y.",
      "displayCode": {
        "c": "for (i = 0; i <= {{C}}; i++)\n  Swap({{D}}, FindMin({{E}}, N-1));"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q8-code",
      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Question 8 · C star function",
      "markdown": "",
      "displayCode": {
        "c": "void f(int i) {\nint j, k;\n\n  j = {{L}};\n  k = {{M}};\n  printf(\"%d and %d\\n\", j, k);\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q9-code",
      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Question 9 · C program segment",
      "markdown": "",
      "displayCode": {
        "c": "printf(\"%d\", A[0]);\nfor (i=0; i<{{N}}; i++)\n  if ({{O}})\n    printf(\"%d\", A[i+1]);"
      }
    }
